{"parentUuid":"a226ae93-0635-499c-94d7-33868949e1e7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2eb72196-1181-458f-823e-509b39a986c1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D5QAzCZRi77eHqzWwowAK5","type":"tool_result","content":"VISION [informational/ste]  (945 words, 1 findings)\n  - passive voice: 4.7% of sentences (max 3.0%); name the actor [heuristic: verify each hit]\n\n1 findings across 1 page(s)\nchain: voicecheck -> /humanizer (tone) -> /slopbeth (slop) -> voicecheck (gate)\nno later stage may reintroduce a finding above","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f4b1f1cd-62ed-489b-b113-13ebe57cc43e","timestamp":"2026-11-12T16:09:51.414Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"VISION [informational/ste]  (945 words, 1 findings)\n  - passive voice: 4.7% of sentences (max 3.0%); name the actor [heuristic: verify each hit]\n\n1 findings across 1 page(s)\nchain: voicecheck -> /humanizer (tone) -> /slopbeth (slop) -> voicecheck (gate)\nno later stage may reintroduce a finding above","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":79,"oldLines":6,"newStart":79,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | D50 | A constraint may be a hook: a command that runs in the job's VM before each matching call at its steps, after the charter's hooks, unless it is only told. Exit 2 refuses the call. An owner's constraint can be removed; a charter's changes in its repository. |"," | D51 | A constraint may name a reviewer from `.agents/agents/`. When its step finishes, the reviewer reads the step's change in a turn with no tools, from its file at the job's base, and its fail fails the step as D47 says. A reviewer that can't run leaves the job with a person. |"," | D52 | A server's MCP servers reach a turn through `workers/bastion-mcp`, which registers each tool as `mcp::<server>::<tool>`. Only MCP servers over HTTP: a stdio server would run on the host, outside the VM. A server's token stays in the vault, and only the bridge may read it. |","+| D53 | A step's rules live with the step, on the Workflows page, in one tab by layer: the charter (read-only, from the repository), the harness (grants, and the rules and hooks on calls), and the factory (review checks and reviewers). With no step picked, the page shows what applies at every step. Each rung is a switch. There is no Constraints or Capabilities page. |"," "," ## Open questions"," "]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/VISION.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":53,"oldLines":10,"newStart":53,"newLines":11,"lines":[" same way on each of these pages. You open a job, an entry or a turn and act"," on it wherever it lives."," ","-**Rules, one server at a time.** Workflows, Constraints, Capabilities,","-Engine and Settings belong to the server you pick. A rules page never mixes","-two servers, because each server's rules shape only its own jobs, and a sum","-of two rule sets means nothing.","+**Rules, one server at a time.** Workflows, Engine and Settings belong to","+the server you pick. A step's rules live on the Workflows page, with the","+step, and what applies at every step shows there when no step is picked. A","+rules page never mixes two servers, because each server's rules shape only","+its own jobs, and a sum of two rule sets means nothing."," "," ## What a server holds"," "]},{"oldStart":66,"oldLines":9,"newStart":67,"newLines":11,"lines":[" - **Workspaces:** the repositories it works in, each with its checks, its","   setup, its VM image, and what happens to a job's branch at the end."," - **Workflows:** its series of steps, each step with its settings.","-- **Capabilities and constraints:** what an agent may call, each grant ask","-  or allowed, and the rules its work must keep, each from told to enforced.","-  Both apply to every step of a kind, or to one workflow step.","+- **Rules, by layer:** the charter each workspace's repository brings; the","+  harness, what an agent may call and the rules and hooks on those calls;","+  and the factory, the checks on the work and the reviewers that must pass.","+  Each grant is ask or allowed, and each constraint is told, checked or","+  enforced. They apply at one workflow step, or at every step."," - **Settings:** its model providers, its people and their roles, its","   notifications, and its secrets."," - **Records:** its jobs, its audit log, its evals, its costs, and what"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/DECISIONS.md","/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion/VISION.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"4f7ea813-97dd-4ab8-98cf-9bae8b53340f","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","root":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","branch":"main","default_branch":"main","status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":1,"modified":4,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a226ae93-0635-499c-94d7-33868949e1e7","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
